{# ============================================================================
   HOST OVERRIDE of @UhifadhiIncident/report/_page.html.twig.

   ONE DIFFERENCE from the module's own copy, and it is the ruling this file
   exists for: step 3 — "People & evidence", its four CAN WAIT sub-rows and the
   "Then, on the record" explainer — is gone, replaced by a single quiet line
   beside the File control. The quick-file discipline is unchanged; only its
   presentation shrank. Everything else below is the module's template verbatim,
   so keep it in step when the bundle moves.

   CONTAINER A — THE FULL PAGE. Standalone filing: a deep link, a fresh tab, the
   dashboard's Report button when it is not anchored to a record.

   A PAGE, NOT AN OVERLAY. Filing an incident is the most consequential thing this
   product asks anybody to do, and it must not be something a click beside it can
   throw away. A route survives a reload, a dropped connection, a second tab and a
   pasted link; it prints; and it is the same address another module's "file as
   incident" button already points at. The steps become plain headed sections down
   one column — there is room, so nothing has to hide.

   The steps themselves are the SHARED partials — the drawer renders the very same
   files at a narrower width.

   Parameters: controller, area, categories, prefill, chosen, csrfToken, errors,
               createUrl, cancelUrl, sourceFiles
   ========================================================================== #}
<div class="crumb"><a href="{{ path('dashboard_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('dashboard_area_show', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ area.name|lower }}</a> / <a href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">incidents</a> / new</div>

<div class="pghead">
    <div>
        <h1 class="pg">Report an incident</h1>
        <p class="pgsub">Three answers file an incident — a kind, one line saying what happened, and a place. How bad it
            was, who was involved, what it cost and anything that shows it can be added here or on the record
            afterwards, where the timeline keeps who added what and when.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pgact w-pgact">
        <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ cancelUrl }}">{{ ux_icon('lucide:chevron-left') }} Back to incidents</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div {{ stimulus_controller(controller) }}>
    {% if prefill.hasProvenance %}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_source.html.twig', {prefill: prefill, files: sourceFiles}, with_context: false) }}
    {% endif %}

    {# input and change both bubble, so ONE action on the form re-reads the gate
       whatever the filer typed into. #}
    <form class="ro-form" method="post" action="{{ createUrl }}"
          {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'input')|stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'change') }}>
        {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_carry.html.twig', {csrfToken: csrfToken, prefill: prefill, errors: errors}, with_context: false) }}

        <div class="ro-sect">
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 1, heading: 'What kind of incident', mark: 'req', markLabel: 'needed to file'}, with_context: false) }}
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_kind.html.twig', {controller: controller, categories: categories, chosen: chosen, compact: false}, with_context: false) }}
        </div>

        <div class="ro-sect">
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 2, heading: 'What happened', mark: null, markLabel: null}, with_context: false) }}
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_what.html.twig', {controller: controller, categories: categories, chosen: chosen, prefill: prefill, compact: false}, with_context: false) }}
        </div>

        {# THE THINGS THAT CAN WAIT ARE ONE LINE HERE, not a section. The module
           ships a third step for them; this deployment says the same thing in a
           sentence beside the File control, because a filer at the roadside reads
           the discipline once and then files. Nothing about the discipline
           changed — only how much screen it costs to be told it. #}
        <p class="use">Only the kind, what happened and where are needed now. Severity, people, evidence and money are
            added on the record afterwards.</p>

        {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_gate.html.twig', {controller: controller, chosen: chosen, prefill: prefill, cancelUrl: cancelUrl, compact: false}, with_context: false) }}
    </form>
</div>

<div class="c i-rules">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">IN·RO</span>The rules the form enforces<span class="src">· the container may change; these do not</span></span>
    <div class="rln"><span>Required to file</span><span class="mono acc">a category · one line saying what happened · a place</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span>Never required</span><span class="mono">how bad, people, evidence, money — they follow on the record</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span>The File control</span><span class="mono">dead until the required answers exist · the server refuses the same filing</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span>Starting state</span><span class="mono">reported — never verified</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span>Provenance</span><span class="mono">written once, never editable</span></div>
    <div class="use">A report is cheap and a verification is expensive. Filing may never cost more than those three
        answers — and an incomplete report may never reach a register that cannot hold it.</div>
</div>
